Native VU1: clean-operand analysis across blocks (after rac-rs tools/vu/vuclean.py, AsobiCodes/rac-rs).
- vu1n_gen.py: a VF lane is clean when its exponent is not 255; reading it with vu1n::ld instead of vu1n::ldn (which turns
  Inf/NaN into +-FLT_MAX) gives the same value. Every pair has one affine effect (pair_effect: lanes made clean by
  ADD/SUB/MUL/MADD/MSUB/MAX/MINI/ITOF, lanes made unknown by every other VF write, now also FTOI/ABS/exact-engine upper ops
  and the upper op of a branch pair, which the per-block tracking left marked clean). Per micro-memory a forward fixpoint
  over the static control flow (meet = AND) gives each block's entry state, ANDed over every image the block is in; the
  block is compiled for it and registers its masks (VU1NativeLanes: req = entry lanes it reads unnormalised, gen / keep =
  its effect). 9,833 -> 6,273 normalised operand loads.
- Runtime (runNative): the lanes known clean are tracked along the blocks actually run (known = (known & keep) | gen,
  vf00 always); a block whose req is not all known gets its lanes checked in the registers (vu1n::lanesClean) and runs in
  the exact engine if one is not clean. So the result never depends on the analysis being complete (new micro-memories,
  jumps through registers, exact-engine stretches). GOW_VU1N_DIAG prints laneChecks / laneFails.
Verified on the ship with the launcher's defaults: GOW_VU1N_VERIFY=20000 0 mismatches against the exact engine, 11.8 M lane
checks 0 failures. With 10 and 11: combat average 56.5 -> 58.8 fps, minimum 51.4 -> 56.0.

