+#
+# A VF lane is clean when its exponent is not 255 (no Inf / NaN bits): reading it through vu1n::ldn (which turns exponent
+# 255 into +-FLT_MAX, like the exact engine's operand normalisation) gives the same value as a plain vu1n::ld. State: a
+# 128-bit mask, bit r*4 + lane (SSE lane order, bit 0 = x) set when VF r's lane is known clean. Results of ADD / SUB / MUL
+# / MADD / MSUB (clamped), MAX / MINI (of normalised operands) and ITOF are clean; every other VF write (lower ops, FTOI,
+# ABS, ops run by the exact engine) makes the register unknown. A pair's effect is affine (lanes set, cleared or kept),
+# so a block is summarised by gen (clean on exit whatever the entry) and keep (unchanged by the block).
+ALL_LANES = (1 << 128) - 1
+VF0_LANES = 0xF  # vf00 = (0, 0, 0, 1): always clean
